      {
        "id": 117041,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-09-05T23:09:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The recharge mode section says he is losing 2 phases on his first turn. However since Recharge Mode also gives damage reduction of 1, wouldn't that mean only the Power Phase is lost, as his play gave him a benefit outside of only drawing cards? It's equal to playing Heavy Plating and using Initialize in the same turn, the only difference is following round, where Bunker can draw 3 if Recharge Mode is in play.</p><p>Mistform also provides a gameplay benefit outside of just drawing cards.</p><p>Also Prayer of Desperation. It is possible to draw 0 cards from it.</p><p>Kill On Sight, perhaps a note stating that the target actually has to be removed from play to gain the benefits of the drawing?</p><p>Supply Crate&nbsp;seems to be under the assumption that Unity is able to use a power, either by already having a COnstruction Pylon or Modular Workbench in play, another option being she destroys someone else's equipment card. If none of these conditions are able to be met, then she would be losing her Power Phase as well. Brainstorm also falls under this.</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:49:37.433Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
